    "narrative": "For the May 29th slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** is the clear anchor of our lineup with a 74.98 efficiency score. Despite facing a left-handed matchup, his elite base projection and favorable spot in the two-hole make him an automatic start. He is joined by the reliable pair of **Matt Chapman** (69.75) and **Luis Arraez** (69.53), who benefit significantly from a park factor boost and favorable matchups against Lorenzen. While **Jonathan Aranda** lands just behind them at 66.12, his placement in the two-hole against Ure\u00f1a creates a strong Roto foundation. **Taylor Ward** represents our highest-upside play among the outfielders; despite a tough matchup against Macko, his lead-off status and extreme park advantage push his score to 59.23, making him a primary source for potential runs.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Bryson Stott**, who fell just short of the starting criteria with a 45.06 score. While his potential for stolen bases is tempting given our league\u2019s focus on that scarcity, the combination of a difficult matchup against Wrobleski and the negative impact of his platoon split kept him out of the primary nine. We are exercising caution with **Geraldo Perdomo** and **Will Smith** today, as their scores are anchored by daunting matchups against Kirby and Wheeler, respectively. **Daulton Varsho** and **Tyler Freeman** remain in the lineup as marginal plays, relying on park factors to offset the talent gap of their opposing pitchers. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz** on the IL, while **Lawrence Butler**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, **Gleyber Torres**, and **Drew Gilbert** remain on the bench as we preserve our game caps for more favorable daily efficiency windows.",
